WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.480 --> 00:00:01.510
- Look at me.

00:00:01.510 --> 00:00:02.450
- Okay honey.

00:00:02.450 --> 00:00:04.344
- Why you no look at me anymore?

00:00:04.344 --> 00:00:05.483
- I am looking.

00:00:05.483 --> 00:00:06.380
- You, I'm over here.

00:00:06.380 --> 00:00:08.500
- I know, but look on the
T.V. I'm looking at ya.

00:00:08.500 --> 00:00:09.921
- Oh yes, very good.

00:00:09.921 --> 00:00:11.662
(laughter)

00:00:11.662 --> 00:00:13.346
- I understand everything.

00:00:13.346 --> 00:00:16.096
(mystical music)

00:00:19.820 --> 00:00:21.380
- Puppetry's a funny art because you don't

00:00:21.380 --> 00:00:23.030
really notice it, unless it's wrong.

00:00:23.030 --> 00:00:25.880
So in anything, in theater,
or in film or television,

00:00:25.880 --> 00:00:26.947
if it's wrong you're like

00:00:26.947 --> 00:00:29.080
"that thing looks weird,
he's just broke his neck

00:00:29.080 --> 00:00:30.190
the way he looked round there."

00:00:30.190 --> 00:00:33.110
So but when it's right you
shouldn't think about it,

00:00:33.110 --> 00:00:34.800
like Louis says, you shouldn't
really think about puppets.

00:00:34.800 --> 00:00:36.590
Once you've got in the
zone of Dark Crystal,

00:00:36.590 --> 00:00:38.227
when you watch episode one and you go

00:00:38.227 --> 00:00:40.007
"Okay, that's how they are,
that's how that tribe is

00:00:40.007 --> 00:00:41.250
and that's how these guys are."

00:00:41.250 --> 00:00:42.350
Then you forget that, hopefully,

00:00:42.350 --> 00:00:43.300
and that all just falls away.

00:00:43.300 --> 00:00:45.470
Like when you watch Nick
Parks stuff, you know?

00:00:45.470 --> 00:00:47.930
You don't go "Oh, well this
is made out of plasticine."

00:00:47.930 --> 00:00:51.830
You know, you just fall
in, you buy into that world

00:00:51.830 --> 00:00:53.300
like in cartoons or whatever.

00:00:53.300 --> 00:00:56.010
- And we're so aware of the
skeleton and the gravity.

00:00:56.010 --> 00:00:57.780
You know, so like things
shouldn't bend the wrong way

00:00:57.780 --> 00:00:59.182
because that's an injury.

00:00:59.182 --> 00:01:01.463
(laughter)

00:01:01.463 --> 00:01:02.360
We're constantly aware of that.

00:01:02.360 --> 00:01:03.610
- Yeah, we should show the polling.

00:01:03.610 --> 00:01:05.692
Maybe it's because some
of these points are better

00:01:05.692 --> 00:01:07.300
to be illustrated with
the real thing, right?

00:01:07.300 --> 00:01:08.540
- You have the Skeksis,
you have the Gelfling,

00:01:08.540 --> 00:01:09.786
and also the Podlings as well.

00:01:09.786 --> 00:01:12.090
- [Dave] Yeah, Podlings are
great fun all day and all night.

00:01:12.090 --> 00:01:13.240
Everyone loves a Podling. (laughter)

00:01:13.240 --> 00:01:14.890
If you detail someone a Podling,

00:01:14.890 --> 00:01:16.531
like "Hey, Fred, today you're a Podling."

00:01:16.531 --> 00:01:17.731
They go "Yay.

00:01:17.731 --> 00:01:20.533
- Cha-ching.

00:01:20.533 --> 00:01:23.160
- All the Gelfling shots
are hard, no question.

00:01:23.160 --> 00:01:24.560
Everything about a Gelfling does is hard.

00:01:24.560 --> 00:01:26.520
- [Warrick] It takes
so much concentration.

00:01:26.520 --> 00:01:27.490
- [Dave] Yeah, and stillness.

00:01:27.490 --> 00:01:29.170
And then a Podling I
light them up at show,

00:01:29.170 --> 00:01:30.300
which we'll show you in a minute because

00:01:30.300 --> 00:01:31.580
it's all big and broad and funny.

00:01:31.580 --> 00:01:34.250
And Skeksis like pantover
because they are again

00:01:34.250 --> 00:01:38.180
big and you have to turn
a Skeksis around and

00:01:38.180 --> 00:01:39.658
look down the lense and it's terrifying.

00:01:39.658 --> 00:01:41.600
And they're huge as well,
that's the other thing.

00:01:41.600 --> 00:01:45.630
The Empress is about 7'2", 7'3"
once I'm in it and it's on.

00:01:45.630 --> 00:01:47.787
Like, people come to
the set and grown men,

00:01:47.787 --> 00:01:50.645
they look at them like "Oh
my God, it's terrifying."

00:01:50.645 --> 00:01:51.478
(laughter)

00:01:51.478 --> 00:01:53.090
- Because they're also up in the air.

00:01:53.090 --> 00:01:53.923
- Because they have the
memory from their childhood.

00:01:54.790 --> 00:01:55.623
(laughter)

00:01:55.623 --> 00:01:56.900
- All the nightmares come flooding back.

00:01:56.900 --> 00:01:58.537
- We had two days in the
Podling wayhouse which is

00:01:58.537 --> 00:02:00.837
the Podling pub, and it
was the best two days.

00:02:01.970 --> 00:02:04.760
We just skipped around,
singing and dancing and

00:02:04.760 --> 00:02:07.220
there was like beer jugs
with foam on top and

00:02:07.220 --> 00:02:09.690
we were flinging the foam
at each other and stuff.

00:02:09.690 --> 00:02:11.360
- It was like a jamboree of like how many

00:02:11.360 --> 00:02:13.330
site guys can we get
in this scene, ya know?

00:02:13.330 --> 00:02:15.590
Like, this guy's drunk, he falls over,

00:02:15.590 --> 00:02:17.520
his wife punches him in the face, ya know.

00:02:17.520 --> 00:02:19.220
So many things, they're
not all in the show but

00:02:19.220 --> 00:02:20.110
we did have such a giggle.

00:02:20.110 --> 00:02:21.785
- [Warrick] But then
because it's so much fun

00:02:21.785 --> 00:02:23.328
you want to do it all the time.

00:02:23.328 --> 00:02:25.390
So you guys can't see it,
but we know that we're the

00:02:25.390 --> 00:02:27.147
two Podlings over here and
then in the reverse we're like

00:02:27.147 --> 00:02:28.200
"Oh no, I'm doing that one."

00:02:28.200 --> 00:02:29.610
So then we're over here doing
this and then we're up there

00:02:29.610 --> 00:02:31.550
doing the musicians, we're
just all over the place.

00:02:31.550 --> 00:02:33.250
- Yeah. But that's another weird
thing, you talk to yourself

00:02:33.250 --> 00:02:34.854
so there's sequences
where, because we play

00:02:34.854 --> 00:02:36.420
multiple characters in the show--

00:02:36.420 --> 00:02:38.740
- [Chris] Like when Autumn
talks to the Emperor.

00:02:38.740 --> 00:02:41.010
- [Dave] Yeah, Autumn comes
and talks to the Emperor

00:02:41.010 --> 00:02:43.080
so there's this whole thing
of like I must order the

00:02:43.080 --> 00:02:44.790
shot where he's really thinking,

00:02:44.790 --> 00:02:46.340
it's a very powerful moment in the show.

00:02:46.340 --> 00:02:48.560
And then of course, you
just get that off your sheet

00:02:48.560 --> 00:02:50.067
and it's like half past 11 in
the morning and you're like

00:02:50.067 --> 00:02:51.250
"Whew, got that out of the way."

00:02:51.250 --> 00:02:53.470
And then of course you got to
flip it and get in the Emperor

00:02:53.470 --> 00:02:55.280
and do the other side
of that shot and talk to

00:02:55.280 --> 00:02:56.880
somebody else standing in for you.

00:02:56.880 --> 00:02:59.030
And it's just continuous, just relentless.

00:02:59.030 --> 00:03:00.975
- And then you need therapy all night.

00:03:00.975 --> 00:03:01.960
(laughter)

00:03:01.960 --> 00:03:04.040
- [Chris] It looked heavy
as well because when you're

00:03:04.040 --> 00:03:07.976
inside the Skeksis as well
you're strapped in essentially,

00:03:07.976 --> 00:03:09.610
you have the monitor as well.

00:03:09.610 --> 00:03:11.640
- They're very heavy. Like
you said, we've got the straps

00:03:11.640 --> 00:03:13.270
and we've got the everything.

00:03:13.270 --> 00:03:15.280
So it keeps the body up, you
don't have to hold the body up.

00:03:15.280 --> 00:03:17.280
The body is just suspended
in mid-air because

00:03:17.280 --> 00:03:18.167
it's attached to your body.

00:03:18.167 --> 00:03:20.170
And the head's heavy, and
the head's just resting on

00:03:20.170 --> 00:03:21.500
the back of your hand,
because there's all the

00:03:21.500 --> 00:03:22.630
animatronics inside there.

00:03:22.630 --> 00:03:24.580
And then you get into
the armor for the battle,

00:03:24.580 --> 00:03:27.314
and the blades and the wings and stuff.

00:03:27.314 --> 00:03:30.060
So yeah, like it's just to sweat you down.

00:03:30.060 --> 00:03:31.118
We were sweating down
to or knees some days.

00:03:31.118 --> 00:03:32.730
(Chris laughs)

00:03:32.730 --> 00:03:34.624
- [Dave] And also the other
is a standard creature suit.

00:03:34.624 --> 00:03:36.976
A standard creature suit is
pretty hot, but this is because

00:03:36.976 --> 00:03:39.360
of the beautiful design
of Brian and beautiful

00:03:39.360 --> 00:03:42.010
costume designers, you've
got a cotton and then

00:03:42.010 --> 00:03:43.949
a crinoline, then the
fabric, then a gauze,

00:03:43.949 --> 00:03:46.610
then like the great ruffs and the ruffles.

00:03:46.610 --> 00:03:48.376
All the jewelry, the chains.

00:03:48.376 --> 00:03:51.140
The Emperor has these
heavy gloves and rings and

00:03:51.140 --> 00:03:53.020
the cape, and everything.

00:03:53.020 --> 00:03:54.950
- But all those textures are great in 4K.

00:03:54.950 --> 00:03:56.640
- Yeah it looks great, yeah.

00:03:56.640 --> 00:03:57.473
- It's worth it.

00:03:57.473 --> 00:03:59.050
Like, I had to wait until
I saw the series and

00:03:59.050 --> 00:04:00.110
I was like "Okay yeah, it was worth it."

00:04:00.110 --> 00:04:02.487
- Yeah it does, it looks
cool but it's heavy.

00:04:02.487 --> 00:04:03.320
And hot.

00:04:03.320 --> 00:04:04.870
- So the Podlings are
so much fun so we should

00:04:04.870 --> 00:04:05.845
get some of that.

00:04:05.845 --> 00:04:07.389
- Yeah, we should get some Podling time.

00:04:07.389 --> 00:04:09.350
- [Dave] The first thing
with puppets is eye focus,

00:04:09.350 --> 00:04:10.610
where other puppets are looking.

00:04:10.610 --> 00:04:11.780
So obviously we were
goofing around earlier,

00:04:11.780 --> 00:04:12.970
we're looking straight down the lense,

00:04:12.970 --> 00:04:15.280
which is much more like
live television puppetry.

00:04:15.280 --> 00:04:18.023
- Hello, welcome to the Podling show.

00:04:18.023 --> 00:04:19.227
- Welcome to the Podling show.

00:04:19.227 --> 00:04:20.890
- Yeah, we're Podlings.

00:04:20.890 --> 00:04:22.390
- Today I will cook for you.

00:04:22.390 --> 00:04:23.223
- No don't, please.

00:04:23.223 --> 00:04:24.056
- No?

00:04:24.056 --> 00:04:24.889
- No.

00:04:24.889 --> 00:04:25.722
- Okay fine.

00:04:25.722 --> 00:04:27.350
- [Dave] So we don't use
that in The Dark Crystal,

00:04:27.350 --> 00:04:29.060
they never look down the lense obviously.

00:04:29.060 --> 00:04:30.900
- [Warrick] No, because
they live in the real world.

00:04:30.900 --> 00:04:31.746
(laughter)

00:04:31.746 --> 00:04:33.330
- But it's that thing of,
well they talk to each other.

00:04:33.330 --> 00:04:34.163
- Yes.

00:04:34.163 --> 00:04:35.640
- Yes, so I'm looking at you now.

00:04:35.640 --> 00:04:36.740
- Yes, you look at me.

00:04:37.910 --> 00:04:39.040
- [Warrick] We cheat on the
eye lines a hell of a lot

00:04:39.040 --> 00:04:40.650
because this isn't interesting.

00:04:40.650 --> 00:04:42.420
You know, seeing that
profile of the character's

00:04:42.420 --> 00:04:44.600
not interesting, so what I'm
doing there is not interesting.

00:04:44.600 --> 00:04:46.490
But what Dave's doing is
showing you both of those eyes.

00:04:46.490 --> 00:04:47.323
- Oh yeah, yeah.

00:04:47.323 --> 00:04:49.860
So I'm talking to my wife
but I'm talking weirdly,

00:04:49.860 --> 00:04:50.831
kind of throwing my eyes around and then

00:04:50.831 --> 00:04:53.930
if you see two eyes it
brings the characters alive.

00:04:53.930 --> 00:04:55.080
- You see we tilt the
head ever so slightly

00:04:55.080 --> 00:04:56.630
because in 2D it works well.

00:04:56.630 --> 00:04:57.760
On the screen, it works well.

00:04:57.760 --> 00:04:58.770
- Yeah, that's right.

00:04:58.770 --> 00:05:00.390
And then weirdly sometimes because of the

00:05:00.390 --> 00:05:02.426
prohibitive nature of set
design on any production,

00:05:02.426 --> 00:05:03.653
you can cheat it.

00:05:04.750 --> 00:05:06.811
I mean, in reality I
can be looking way pa--

00:05:06.811 --> 00:05:09.170
like, if you look at
where we are we're not

00:05:09.170 --> 00:05:10.180
actually really looking at each other.

00:05:10.180 --> 00:05:11.427
- Look at me.

00:05:11.427 --> 00:05:12.260
- Okay, hunny.

00:05:12.260 --> 00:05:13.692
- Why you no look at me anymore?

00:05:13.692 --> 00:05:14.579
(laughter)

00:05:14.579 --> 00:05:15.412
- I am looking at you.

00:05:15.412 --> 00:05:16.245
- You, I'm over here.

00:05:16.245 --> 00:05:17.133
- I know, look on the TV.

00:05:17.133 --> 00:05:18.080
I am looking at you.

00:05:18.080 --> 00:05:19.677
- Oh yes, very good.

00:05:19.677 --> 00:05:21.459
(laughter)

00:05:21.459 --> 00:05:23.242
I understand everything, yes.

00:05:23.242 --> 00:05:25.350
- Okay so, what about near and far?

00:05:25.350 --> 00:05:26.183
Near and far?

00:05:26.183 --> 00:05:27.016
- Oh yeah,

00:05:27.016 --> 00:05:28.115
- So stay foreground?

00:05:28.115 --> 00:05:28.948
- Yeah.

00:05:28.948 --> 00:05:30.607
- Okay, well you can run
with this if you want

00:05:30.607 --> 00:05:31.800
but just quickly.

00:05:31.800 --> 00:05:35.568
Puppets, for some crazy
reason, if I had a human being

00:05:35.568 --> 00:05:37.930
here right now and I
took them this far away,

00:05:37.930 --> 00:05:39.610
they don't go that small.

00:05:39.610 --> 00:05:42.320
But because the puppets are
already small, smaller than a

00:05:42.320 --> 00:05:44.620
human, you can put them there
and we're the same size.

00:05:44.620 --> 00:05:47.170
And then just two or three
paces I look like I'm

00:05:47.170 --> 00:05:48.003
20 feet away from him.

00:05:48.003 --> 00:05:49.040
- How you shrinking?

00:05:49.040 --> 00:05:52.550
- Oh no, I feel really weird
like you look like a monster.

00:05:52.550 --> 00:05:53.383
- Watch this, folks.

00:05:53.383 --> 00:05:55.290
- Watch it on the TV, don't
watch it in reality, okay?

00:05:55.290 --> 00:05:56.744
- Watch it on the TV, oh shut up!

00:05:56.744 --> 00:05:57.577
(laughter)

00:05:57.577 --> 00:05:58.410
- It's a gag, watch on the screen.

00:05:58.410 --> 00:05:59.584
Here we go.

00:05:59.584 --> 00:06:00.417
- Okay, I start again.

00:06:00.417 --> 00:06:01.489
Watch it on the TV, folks.

00:06:01.489 --> 00:06:02.322
- Yeah, good.

00:06:02.322 --> 00:06:03.571
I'm scared of you, you look big and scary

00:06:03.571 --> 00:06:05.979
(puppet one roars, puppet two screams)

00:06:05.979 --> 00:06:08.324
(audience laughs)

00:06:08.324 --> 00:06:11.310
- (spits) Boney.

00:06:11.310 --> 00:06:13.621
- Yeah, it's a optical illusion.

00:06:13.621 --> 00:06:17.472
- [Dave] Yeah so, we play with
depth of field all the time.

00:06:17.472 --> 00:06:19.017
- So we're going to talk about walks--

00:06:19.017 --> 00:06:19.850
- No, hang on.

00:06:19.850 --> 00:06:20.683
Before we do that,
little creature flies by.

00:06:20.683 --> 00:06:21.516
Eye focus.

00:06:22.717 --> 00:06:24.640
- This is really hard for me.

00:06:24.640 --> 00:06:25.500
- Who's leading, you?

00:06:25.500 --> 00:06:26.333
- No.

00:06:26.333 --> 00:06:27.334
- Okay, I'll lead.

00:06:27.334 --> 00:06:28.167
(laughter)

00:06:28.167 --> 00:06:29.970
- [Dave] So all we're doing
is we're going to follow

00:06:29.970 --> 00:06:32.050
a little creature fly around the screen.

00:06:32.050 --> 00:06:33.587
- Wow, look at it.

00:06:33.587 --> 00:06:35.425
- And we're not really
doing anything much,

00:06:35.425 --> 00:06:38.980
but we're both looking in
unison and that means..

00:06:38.980 --> 00:06:39.813
- So pretty.

00:06:39.813 --> 00:06:41.065
- Yes, isn't she beautiful?

00:06:41.065 --> 00:06:42.340
- Can I eat it?

00:06:42.340 --> 00:06:43.253
- No, don't eat it.

00:06:43.253 --> 00:06:44.086
- Okay.

00:06:44.086 --> 00:06:46.679
- I want to put a pin throuhg
her and stick it on my wall.

00:06:46.679 --> 00:06:47.884
(audience laughs)

00:06:47.884 --> 00:06:49.370
That's what they do.

00:06:49.370 --> 00:06:51.422
- Let's have it come through the middle,

00:06:51.422 --> 00:06:52.255
right down the middle.

00:06:52.255 --> 00:06:54.984
- Oh, oh (chomp) I couldn't resist.

00:06:54.984 --> 00:06:57.800
(laughter)

00:06:57.800 --> 00:07:00.762
- So but you can see
that those movements are

00:07:00.762 --> 00:07:03.260
very, very, very small.

00:07:03.260 --> 00:07:06.180
Like again, lots of
puppeteers who's thought..

00:07:06.180 --> 00:07:07.013
(Podling choking)

00:07:07.013 --> 00:07:08.292
- What's wrong with you?

00:07:08.292 --> 00:07:09.605
(Podling vomits)

00:07:09.605 --> 00:07:10.438
(laughter)

00:07:10.438 --> 00:07:11.271
- Come on.

00:07:11.271 --> 00:07:12.104
- Who is disgusting?

00:07:12.104 --> 00:07:12.937
- Look at all these
people are watching us,

00:07:12.937 --> 00:07:13.840
we got to be professional.

00:07:13.840 --> 00:07:14.733
- I very sorry.

00:07:14.733 --> 00:07:17.993
- There's a thing of people
put puppets on and go

00:07:17.993 --> 00:07:19.730
(mumbles)

00:07:19.730 --> 00:07:20.690
- Ah, that's great.

00:07:20.690 --> 00:07:22.125
- Yeah, right? Thanks.

00:07:22.125 --> 00:07:23.170
(audience laughs)

00:07:23.170 --> 00:07:24.518
- But it's actually, it's very small.

00:07:24.518 --> 00:07:27.030
Even sometimes Podlings are small.

00:07:27.030 --> 00:07:29.490
Gelfling are very very small
as we were saying a minute ago,

00:07:29.490 --> 00:07:30.323
in their movements.

00:07:30.323 --> 00:07:31.375
- You couldn't do any
of this with a Gelfling,

00:07:31.375 --> 00:07:32.547
you would not be laughing.

00:07:32.547 --> 00:07:33.860
- I would be nervous or weird.

00:07:33.860 --> 00:07:35.673
- [Warrick] You'd leave, I think.

00:07:35.673 --> 00:07:36.506
(laughter)

00:07:36.506 --> 00:07:38.374
- [Dave] So do you want
to go to walks now?

00:07:38.374 --> 00:07:39.292
- [Warrick] Yeah.

00:07:39.292 --> 00:07:40.391
- [Dave] So we're going
to talk about the walks.

00:07:40.391 --> 00:07:41.350
This is a Gelfling walk on a Podling.

00:07:41.350 --> 00:07:42.680
- I'm going to see if this
works, because this is...

00:07:42.680 --> 00:07:43.900
- [Dave] I don't think it
will, but it will be fun.

00:07:43.900 --> 00:07:44.920
We can fail together.

00:07:44.920 --> 00:07:46.468
- It looks like I'm wearing a nappy.

00:07:46.468 --> 00:07:50.720
- [Dave] That's Rian's walk

00:07:50.720 --> 00:07:52.129
- [Warrick] I don't know if that works.

00:07:52.129 --> 00:07:53.090
- [Dave] That is Rian's
walk, but it looks weird

00:07:53.090 --> 00:07:54.508
in a Podling.

00:07:54.508 --> 00:07:55.837
- [Warrick] That's kind of what
he does, and when he does it

00:07:55.837 --> 00:07:58.014
it looks like the gravity is really there.

00:07:58.014 --> 00:08:00.163
- [Dave] Yeah, it's just
'cause they're slightly taller.

00:08:00.163 --> 00:08:02.609
- Which way's the exit?

00:08:02.609 --> 00:08:03.442
(laughter)

00:08:03.442 --> 00:08:06.643
- So, but then here is
a standard muppet walk.

00:08:06.643 --> 00:08:08.850
It's so important to think
about the puppets feet

00:08:08.850 --> 00:08:09.766
on the floor.

00:08:09.766 --> 00:08:12.060
- To give us life.

00:08:12.060 --> 00:08:16.466
- You know, well let's just
walk through both together.

00:08:16.466 --> 00:08:18.924
(Podling wife hums)

00:08:18.924 --> 00:08:19.757
(audience laughs)

00:08:19.757 --> 00:08:20.593
- I'm sorry.

00:08:20.593 --> 00:08:21.543
I'm serious, come on do it again.

00:08:21.543 --> 00:08:22.380
- No it's fine, it's fine.

00:08:22.380 --> 00:08:24.180
But like, we've all
decided where the floor is,

00:08:24.180 --> 00:08:26.180
so if someone's gonna come in
after you they're already--

00:08:26.180 --> 00:08:27.630
- Oh yeah, so let's do it badly.

00:08:27.630 --> 00:08:28.470
- Oh, you want to do it badly?

00:08:28.470 --> 00:08:29.370
- Yeah.

00:08:29.370 --> 00:08:30.203
- Oh, so I do?

00:08:30.203 --> 00:08:31.036
- You're walking properly.

00:08:31.036 --> 00:08:31.869
- Okay, I'm walking properly.

00:08:31.869 --> 00:08:33.197
So I'm here, that's where
I've decided the floor is.

00:08:33.197 --> 00:08:36.160
Next character, what's going on with her?

00:08:36.160 --> 00:08:37.097
(laughter)

00:08:37.097 --> 00:08:37.930
What are you doing?

00:08:37.930 --> 00:08:38.849
- Sorry, I was on my knees.

00:08:38.849 --> 00:08:41.410
- So again, that's where we're
talking about buffalo shoes

00:08:41.410 --> 00:08:44.150
and apple boxes bringing
everyone up to the same floor.

00:08:44.150 --> 00:08:45.880
- And that is kind of the
reason why you need the

00:08:45.880 --> 00:08:47.264
best puppeteers and you
need people who are really

00:08:47.264 --> 00:08:49.420
dedicated to making the craft the best.

00:08:49.420 --> 00:08:51.610
Because you can't afford
to be starting a scene and

00:08:51.610 --> 00:08:53.960
having people do that,
and entering down here.

00:08:53.960 --> 00:08:54.793
- [Dave] No.

00:08:54.793 --> 00:08:55.909
What about waddle?

00:08:55.909 --> 00:08:58.235
Do you have a waddle thing?

00:08:58.235 --> 00:08:59.340
- Oh yeah, this is what I like to do.

00:08:59.340 --> 00:09:00.177
To show off.

00:09:01.590 --> 00:09:03.583
This impresses some people, not everybody.

00:09:03.583 --> 00:09:07.250
(audience laughs, whistles)

00:09:08.640 --> 00:09:10.557
- Oh yes, that's right.

00:09:11.769 --> 00:09:12.770
- And sometimes you'll do your
hands on your hips like that.

00:09:12.770 --> 00:09:13.603
- Oh yeah, go ahead.

00:09:13.603 --> 00:09:17.066
- Sometimes we do one hand
each, but very often you have

00:09:17.066 --> 00:09:19.750
like me here, I'm doing both hands.

00:09:19.750 --> 00:09:21.870
- We're gonna be sassy now.

00:09:21.870 --> 00:09:23.390
- Well we think, we
haven't rehearsed this.

00:09:23.390 --> 00:09:24.580
- It's Friday night,
we're gonna get sassy.

00:09:24.580 --> 00:09:25.660
(laughter)

00:09:25.660 --> 00:09:26.493
- Like we rehearsed it.

00:09:26.493 --> 00:09:27.383
Okay, lets go.

00:09:30.567 --> 00:09:33.723
(audience laughs, cheers)

00:09:33.723 --> 00:09:34.640
- Eh, baby.

00:09:38.227 --> 00:09:40.082
(audience laughs loudly)

00:09:40.082 --> 00:09:41.669
(applause)

00:09:41.669 --> 00:09:45.919
- [Dave] The sassy walk,
they like the sassy walk.

